1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:06,900
This is Hex Machina. It is a debugger for executable graphs,

2
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:12,400
and a browser agent is about to drive it through seven WebMCP tools.

3
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:17,600
The page registers those tools on document.modelContext.

4
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:22,800
Everything you are about to see is the agent calling them. Nobody is clicking.

5
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:28,700
First it inspects the live graph, then it casts the spell.

6
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:34,500
The spell should water a moonflower. Instead, twelve ducks flood the observatory.

7
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:40,400
Now it traces the effect. This is a bounded graph traversal, not a guess.

8
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:46,300
It returns the ordered causal path and every edge responsible for it.

9
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:51,500
Then it proves the diagnosis.

10
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:56,700
The explanation returns the smallest subgraph and proves each edge is necessary.

11
00:00:56,700 --> 00:01:02,300
Here is the part that matters. A human says something the graph cannot infer:

12
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:08,000
the ducks are funny, they stay. That becomes an executable constraint.

13
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,800
The cheapest repair deletes the duck branch entirely.

14
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:21,600
With the constraint locked, it is ineligible, so the agent ranks a longer repair.

15
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:27,500
Before anything is applied, the human sees the exact operation ledger.

16
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:33,300
Eight graph edits, what is preserved, and what the repair gives up.

17
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:38,000
The patch is simulated first, without touching editor state.

18
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,800
Then it is applied atomically, with its preconditions revalidated.

19
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:49,100
The recast succeeds. All twelve ducks survive, and the room stays dry.

20
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:55,500
The moonflower blooms. The human's preference changed the solution, not just the score.

21
00:01:55,500 --> 00:02:01,800
One more thing, because a polished demo invites one question: is this on rails?

22
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:07,900
The evaluation layer generates ninety-six tasks across three causal rules.

23
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:14,000
Let me load a held-out one, from a rule this run has never seen.

24
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:19,900
Every rune, edge, and effect identifier is freshly remapped. Nothing was memorised.

25
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:25,700
The same seven tools inspect it, cast it, trace it, and explain it.

26
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:30,000
Graph interfaces let people and agents negotiate executable intent,

27
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,300
and the application proves every mutation.
